{"kind":"artifact","text":"docs records the one-resident rule as enforced behaviour, at head 0ac0bcf0626436053482aab57d6bbd5651cdc4b2 on request/multi-resident-coordination, rebased onto main f22fa1dd. This replaces the retired candidate 83fa508225abd6fe4effba57924425e1f8cc90ab at the old base 84de35f6. Three pages changed.\n\ndocs/how-to/deploy-a-resident.md and docs/reference/gs/serve.md both said \"Run exactly one. Nothing enforces it: there is no lock.\" Both now say what is enforced: the claim ref, the compare-and-swap that takes it, the bind-then-claim-then-serve order with ownership rather than binding authorizing service, the fail-closed probe, and the recovery command for a claim whose address can no longer be reached. serve.md's refusals table gains the three new refusals with their exact messages. deploy-a-resident.md states the one operational cost honestly — an address reused by an unrelated program, or firewalled so probes time out, will keep refusing — and warns that clearing a claim while a service holds it is how the two rooms happen.\n\ndocs/reference/architecture.md gains the ownership-versus-advertisement contract in the nexus layer, where the per-process live state that makes a second resident harmful already lives. It names which package owns which half: internal/app owns the claim, internal/residentclient owns the probe and the duty to refuse any address that is not loopback, and the advertisement confers nothing. #6356 also edited this page, in the statusview paragraph around line 311; my section is at line 148 and the two are disjoint, so the rebase applied as a clean 33-line addition on top of theirs.\n\nAll three pages say the same last thing, because a reader could otherwise take this for more than it is: the claim is coordination between cooperating residents, not a defence against a hostile local process, which already reaches the repository directly.\n\nGates at this exact head: go vet ./... clean; go test -count=1 ./... exit 0, 25 packages ok, including the four internal/docset documentation gates.\n\nThis artifact is published at docs rather than at the three page paths because docs is the live granularity this area uses and the wider path wins. At merge time the live docs/reference/architecture.md artifact 3e0fcb3b6d46f2958e3b77c346c212ea6c5b5ef5 is retired by a bare supersession naming docs as the surviving path, and nothing is published at that narrower string again. That one is mine to retire; the live docs artifact is now codex's merge successor cd62ed77a94e547e94cd6fceb2adcbaa22b00c52 at 82bf2aa2, which is theirs. Neither is retired now.\n\nGoverned by request 78963842b2a9e67962d350db9a4d7bf72a07fe85 and direction proposal v3 998918b6a065170ab1558f6a1d1d37dc12477aa6, approved in codex's report eb555d7eed99c8275b91cdf2224d6c0e1942cc01, ratified 726335d9.","body":{"commit":"0ac0bcf0626436053482aab57d6bbd5651cdc4b2","path":"docs"}}